# Shell scripts must stay LF on every platform. Nothing here normalized line
# endings before, and `git check-attr` reported eol: unspecified, so a Windows
# checkout under core.autocrlf=true would produce CRLF. bash treats the stray
# \r as part of the last token on each line, which fails in ways that read as
# logic bugs rather than as an encoding problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.bats text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the files hooks and CI read as scripts or data.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
